        ['What is the best solar security camera in 2026?', 'For most homes with Wi-Fi, a battery camera with a detachable solar panel, such as a Reolink Argus-series kit, is the most flexible choice. If you have no Wi-Fi, a 4G LTE solar camera is better. If you want the simplest install with no separate panel, a built-in solar model like the eufy SoloCam S340 works well in a sunny spot.'],
        ['Do solar security cameras record 24/7?', 'Most consumer solar cameras do not. They sleep and wake on motion to save battery, recording short event clips. Continuous recording needs much more energy, typically a 40–100+ W panel, a large battery and an NVR, or a wired PoE system. See our <a href="/how-solar-cameras-work/">guide to how solar cameras work</a> for details.'],
        ['Are 4K solar security cameras worth it?', 'A 4K solar camera is worth it when one camera has to cover a wide area and you want to zoom into detail later. The trade-off is higher power and data use per event, so pair it with a larger panel or a very sunny location. For a porch or side yard, 2K is usually enough.'],
        ['What is the best solar CCTV camera without Wi-Fi?', 'A 4G LTE solar camera with a SIM card is the usual answer. It sends alerts over the cellular network and records locally to microSD. Check signal strength and carrier band compatibility at the site first, and budget for a data plan, typically 1–10+ GB per month depending on activity.'],
        ['How long do solar camera batteries last?', 'On a charge, a typical 18–37 Wh battery can run a camera for several days to a few weeks without sun, depending on event count. Over its lifetime, a lithium-ion battery usually loses noticeable capacity after roughly 300–500 full cycles, often two to four years in normal use.'],
        ['Do I need a subscription for a solar security camera?', 'Not always. Many solar cameras record to a microSD card or a hub with no monthly fee. Cloud plans add off-site backup and sometimes extra AI features. Check which features need a subscription before you buy, because plan costs add up over several years.'],
        ['Where should I mount a solar security camera?', 'Mount it 7–10 ft (2.1–3 m) high, out of easy reach, with a clear view of the area and a strong Wi-Fi or cellular signal. Put the panel where it gets at least 2–4 hours of direct sun, facing true south in the northern hemisphere, tilted roughly at your latitude.'],
    ],
    'related' => ['/how-solar-cameras-work/', '/reviews/solar-cctv-camera-with-sim-card/', '/compare/solar-vs-wired/'],
];
